/*  Emitting C — the checked program, one statement at a time, as C that calls the runtime
    (`cufet-runtime.h`, the one `cufet build` links).

    ★ Held to what the program PRINTS, not to the C `CodeGenerator` writes (the user's ruling): the
    C here may differ from it freely, and each program built is run and compared with the
    interpreter.

    ★★ `unsupported` rather than a guess. Anything this compiler cannot build yet fails with
    `unsupported\t<what>`, never with C that might print the right thing — the same claim the
    checker makes with its own `unsupported`.

    ★ The tree carries no types, so the emitter keeps its own: the kind of each name it has defined,
    and from those the kind of each expression — as `TypeOf` does in `CodeGenerator`.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object emitter with (the map from text to text kinds, the chase body, the text indent,
        the map from text to node functions, the map from text to node objects, the map from text to node methods,
        the map from text to node interfaces, the map from text to fact specialized,
        the series of node pending-functions, the series of text pending-names,
        the series of map from text to text pending-kinds, the map from text to fact unions,
        the series of text union-order).

    /// An emitter for the program, knowing its functions, objects, methods — a method under
    /// `<object>'s <method>` — and interfaces by name.
    Bind emitter to fresh-emitter, given (the map from text to node functions, the map from text to node objects,
            the map from text to node methods, the map from text to node interfaces):
        Return a new emitter { the kinds a map from text to text, the body a chase, the indent "    ",
            the functions functions, the objects objects, the methods methods, the interfaces interfaces,
            the specialized a map from text to fact, the pending-functions a series of node,
            the pending-names a series of text, the pending-kinds a series of map from text to text,
            the unions a map from text to fact, the union-order a series of text }.
    Done.

    /// An emitter for another body of the same program — every table shared, the copies asked for
    /// included, so a copy one body asks for is built once for all of them.
    Bind emitter to sibling unto emitter:
        Return a new emitter { the kinds a map from text to text, the body a chase, the indent "    ",
            the functions one's functions, the objects one's objects, the methods one's methods,
            the interfaces one's interfaces, the specialized one's specialized,
            the pending-functions one's pending-functions, the pending-names one's pending-names,
            the pending-kinds one's pending-kinds, the unions one's unions, the union-order one's union-order }.
    Done.

    /// What this compiler cannot build yet, as a failure message.
    Bind text to not-built, given (the text what):
        Return "unsupported\t{what}".
    Done.

    /// A Cufet name as a C one: hyphens become underscores, which no Cufet name holds, behind a
    /// prefix that keeps it clear of C's own words.
    Bind text to c-name, given (the text name):
        Return "cv_" joined to cast c-ident on (name).
    Done.

    /// A function's name as C — a prefix of its own, so no value's name can ever meet it.
    Bind text to c-function-name, given (the text name):
        Return "cfn_" joined to cast c-ident on (name).
    Done.

    /// The kind of value a written type stands for, or "void" for none.
    Bind text or failure to kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        If cast is-nothing on (written), return "void".
        If written's kind is "NumberType", return "number".
        If written's kind is "TextType", return "text".
        If written's kind is "FactType", return "fact".
        If written's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define object-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (written, 1)).
            If (the entry for object-name in one's objects) is not void, return "object {object-name}".
            If (the entry for object-name in one's interfaces) is not void, return "interface {object-name}".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {object-name}")).
        Done.
        If written's kind is "UnionType":
            Define cases as a series of text.
            For each inner in (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s children, repeat:
                Define case-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (inner) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-scalar on (case-kind) is false and cast object-of on (case-kind) is "" and cast is-union on (case-kind) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a union holding a {case-kind}")).
                Done.
                Insert case-kind into cases.
            Done.
            Define union as cast union-kind-of on (cases).
            Cast one's register-union on (union).
            Return union.
        Done.
        If written's kind is "SeriesType":
            Define element as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-element-kind on (element), return "series of {element}".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a series of {element}")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {written's kind}")).
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A number as the runtime builds one: its digits, how many of them follow the point, its sign.
    Bind text or failure to number-literal, given (the text written):
        Define sign as 0.
        Define unsigned as written.
        If unsigned starts with "-":
            The sign becomes 1.
            The unsigned becomes the characters from 2 to the end of unsigned.
        Done.
        Define scale as 0.
        Define dot as (the position of "." in unsigned but void is 0).
        If dot is greater than 0, the scale becomes the length of unsigned - dot.
        Define digits as replace "." with "" in unsigned.
        // Nineteen digits fit the low word of the coefficient; more wait for the high one.
        If the length of digits is greater than 19:
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a number of more than nineteen digits")).
        Done.
        // Written without its leading zeros, which C would read as octal.
        Define coefficient as (digits converted to number but void is 0) converted to text.
        Return "cufet_dec_lit(0ULL, {coefficient}ULL, {scale}, {sign})".
    Done.

    /// The kind of value an expression gives: "number", "text", "fact", or "series of" one of them.
    Bind text or failure to kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "NumberLiteral", return "number".
            "StringLiteral" or "TextJoin" or "TextConvert", return "text".
            "BooleanLiteral", return "fact".
            "VariableReference":
                Define known as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) in one's kinds.
                If known is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a name defined where this compiler cannot see it")).
                Return known.
            Done.
            "UnaryExpression":
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "Not", return "fact".
                Return "number".
            Done.
            "BinaryExpression":
                Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
                If operator is "Plus" or operator is "Minus" or operator is "Star" or operator is "Slash" or operator is "Percent":
                    Return "number".
                Done.
                Return "fact".
            Done.
            "CastExpression":
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s kind is "PossessiveAccess":
                    Define method as cast one's method-called on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                    Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (method, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
                    If (the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1), 1)) in one's functions) is void:
                        Define by-argument as cast one's method-by-argument on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                        Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (by-argument, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                Done.
                Define called as cast one's function-called on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (called, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "ObjectLiteral":
                Define object-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
                If (the entry for object-name in one's objects) is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a new {object-name}")).
                Return "object {object-name}".
            Done.
            "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's possessive-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "SeriesLiteral" or "RangeExpression" or "SeriesLength" or "SeriesAccess":
                Return cast one's series-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "IsTypeCheck", return "fact".
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// An expression as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "NumberLiteral", return cast number-literal on ((cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word) or pass the failure off.
            // The tree writes a text with C's own escapes, quotes and all.
            "StringLiteral", return (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
            "BooleanLiteral":
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "true", return "1".
                Return "0".
            Done.
            "VariableReference":
                Cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
                // Inside a method, `one` is the object it was called on, held by its address.
                If name is "one", return "(*cv_one)".
                // A narrowed name reads as its case, or as the smaller union.
                Define narrowed as the entry for "@{name}" in one's kinds but void is "".
                If narrowed is not "", return narrowed.
                Return cast c-name on (name).
            Done.
            "ObjectLiteral", return cast one's c-object-literal on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's c-possessive on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "TextJoin":
                Define left as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Define right as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Return "cufet_str_concat({left}, {right})".
            Done.
            "TextConvert", return cast one's c-text-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            "UnaryExpression":
                Define operand as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
                If operator is "Minus", return "cufet_neg({operand})".
                If operator is "Not", return "(!{operand})".
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator}")).
            Done.
            "BinaryExpression", return cast one's c-binary on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "CastExpression", return cast one's c-call on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "SeriesLiteral" or "RangeExpression" or "SeriesLength" or "SeriesAccess":
                Return cast one's c-series-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "IsTypeCheck", return cast one's c-type-check on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The function a call reaches — one of the program's own, called by its name.
    Bind node or failure to function-called unto emitter, given (the node call):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (call, 1).
        If callee's kind is not "VariableReference":
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of a {callee's kind}")).
        Done.
        Define called as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)) in one's functions.
        If called is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of something other than the program's own function")).
        Return called.
    Done.

    /// A call as C: the function's name and its arguments, in order.
    Bind text or failure to c-call unto emitter, given (the node call):
        If (cast field-of on (call, 1))'s kind is "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's c-method-call on (call) or pass the failure off.
        If (cast field-of on (call, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
            If (the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (call, 1), 1)) in one's functions) is void:
                Cast one's method-by-argument on (call) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's c-method-call on (cast as-method-call on (call)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define called as cast one's function-called on (call) or pass the failure off.
        Define listing as cast one's c-arguments on (cast field-of on (called, 3), cast field-of on (call, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define interface-taking as cast one's takes-interface on (called) or pass the failure off.
        If interface-taking:
            Define copy-name as cast one's c-specialized-name on (called, call) or pass the failure off.
            Return "{copy-name}({listing})".
        Done.
        Return "{cast c-function-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (called, 1)))}({listing})".
    Done.

    /// A call's arguments as C, each as the kind its parameter wants — wrapped into a union where
    /// the parameter is one. One passed for an interface is the object it is.
    Bind text or failure to c-arguments unto emitter, given (the node parameters, the node handed):
        Define listing as "".
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in handed's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define wanted as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (item place of parameters's children, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define argument-c as "".
            If wanted starts with "interface ", the argument-c becomes cast one's c-of on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            Otherwise, the argument-c becomes cast one's c-of-as on (argument, wanted) or pass the failure off.
            If listing is "", the listing becomes argument-c.
            Otherwise, the listing becomes "{listing}, {argument-c}".
        Done.
        Return listing.
    Done.

    /// An expression as C text, whatever its kind — what `converted to text` and a hole make.
    Bind text or failure to c-text-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-scalar on (kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {kind} as text")).
        If kind is "number", return "cufet_text_from_dec({value})".
        If kind is "fact", return "({value} ? \"true\" : \"false\")".
        Return value.
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to c-binary unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define left-side as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        Define left as cast one's c-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-line as (cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word.
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        If (operator is "Equal" or operator is "NotEqual") and (cast is-union on (left-kind) or cast is-union on (right-kind)):
            Return cast one's c-union-equal on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast is-scalar on (left-kind) is false:
            If operator is "Equal", return "({cast c-equal on (left-kind, left, right)})".
            If operator is "NotEqual", return "(!{cast c-equal on (left-kind, left, right)})".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on a {left-kind}")).
        Done.
        If left-kind is "number":
            Judge operator, where it is:
                "Plus", return "cufet_add({left}, {right})".
                "Minus", return "cufet_sub({left}, {right})".
                "Star", return "cufet_mul({left}, {right})".
                "Slash", return "cufet_div({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
                "Percent", return "cufet_mod({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
                "Equal", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
                "NotEqual", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) != 0)".
                "Lt", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) < 0)".
                "Gt", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) > 0)".
                "Lte", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) <= 0)".
                "Gte", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) >= 0)".
                Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on numbers")).
            Done.
        Done.
        If left-kind is "text":
            If operator is "Equal", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
            If operator is "NotEqual", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) != 0)".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on text")).
        Done.
        Judge operator, where it is:
            "And", return "({left} && {right})".
            "Or", return "({left} || {right})".
            "Xor", return "(!!({left}) != !!({right}))".
            "Equal", return "(!!({left}) == !!({right}))".
            "NotEqual", return "(!!({left}) != !!({right}))".
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on facts")).
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The C type a kind of value is held in.
    Bind text to c-type, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-union on (kind), return cast union-c-name on (kind).
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}*".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind)).
        If kind is "number", return "CufetDec".
        If kind is "fact", return "int".
        Return "const char*".
    Done.

    /// The runtime call that writes a value of a kind, without the line's end.
    Bind text to write-call, given (the text kind, the text value):
        If cast is-union on (kind), return "{cast union-c-name on (kind)}_write({value})".
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}_write({value})".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind))}_write({value})".
        If kind is "number", return "cufet_write_number({value})".
        If kind is "fact", return "cufet_write_fact({value})".
        Return "cufet_write_text({value})".
    Done.

    Bind void to line unto emitter, given (the text written):
        Insert one's indent into one's body.
        Insert written into one's body.
        Insert "\n" into one's body.
    Done.

    /// A block's statements, one level in. What a block defines is gone when it ends, so the kinds
    /// of the names are put back as they were.
    Bind void or failure to emit-block unto emitter, given (the node statements):
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Cast one's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
    Done.

    /// Whether `left` and `right`, two values of `kind`, are equal — as C.
    Bind text to c-equal, given (the text kind, the text left, the text right):
        If cast is-union on (kind), return "{cast union-c-name on (kind)}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind))}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If kind is "number", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
        If kind is "text", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
        Return "(!!({left}) == !!({right}))".
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-statement unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "StateStatement":
                Define said as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
                Define value as cast one's c-of on (said) or pass the failure off.
                Define value-kind as cast one's kind-of on (said) or pass the failure off.
                // Locked for the whole line: a `State` is several writes.
                Cast one's line on ("cufet_out_lock(); {cast write-call on (value-kind, value)}; cufet_nl(); cufet_out_unlock();").
            Done.
            "DefineStatement":
                // A `permanently` constant waits for a later slice.
                If (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s word is "true":
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a permanent Define")).
                Done.
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define assigned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
                Define value-kind as cast one's kind-of on (assigned) or pass the failure off.
                // Declared with a type, it holds that type — a union, the value wrapped into it.
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) is false:
                    The value-kind becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (assigned, value-kind) or pass the failure off.
                In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes value-kind.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes value-kind.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
                Cast one's line on ("{cast c-type on (value-kind)} {cast c-name on (name)} = {value};").
            Done.
            "BecomesStatement":
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in one's kinds) is void:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a name defined where this compiler cannot see it")).
                Done.
                // Into what the name is stored as — and a narrowed name is narrowed no more.
                Define stored as cast one's stored-kind on (name).
                Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), stored) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("{cast c-name on (name)} = {value};").
                In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes stored.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
            Done.
            "IfStatement", cast one's emit-if on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "WhileStatement":
                Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("while ({condition}) \{").
                Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("\}").
            Done.
            "RepeatUntilStatement":
                Cast one's line on ("do \{").
                Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("\} while (!({condition}));").
            Done.
            "ReturnStatement":
                Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
                If cast is-nothing on (returned), cast one's line on ("return;").
                Otherwise, cast one's line on ("return {cast one's c-of-as on (returned, the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "") or pass the failure off};").
            Done.
            "CastStatement":
                Define call as cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, 2))).
                Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-call on (call) or pass the failure off};").
            Done.
            "BindStatement", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a function inside a body")).
            // An interface was gathered with the program's declarations, and builds nothing itself.
            "InterfaceDefinition", return.
            // A pull's functions and objects are the program's, gathered with its own; what is left
            // is a block. A region frees nothing yet — see emit-pulled.
            "PullStatement" or "PullRabbitStatement", cast one's emit-pulled on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "ObjectDefinition", return a failure (cast not-built on ("an object defined inside a body")).
            "PossessiveSetStatement", cast one's emit-field-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "StopStatement", cast one's line on ("break;").
            "SkipStatement", cast one's line on ("continue;").
            "JudgeStatement", cast one's emit-judge on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "ForEachStatement" or "SeriesInsertStatement" or "SeriesRemoveAtStatement" or "SeriesRemoveValueStatement"
                    or "SeriesSetStatement":
                Cast one's emit-series-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `Pull … Done.` — a block, with the functions and objects in it gathered as the program's.
    /// ⚠ `Pull a rabbit.` is a region, and a region here FREES NOTHING yet: a value made in it and
    /// kept outside it — copied out by C#, which the checked tree does not say — would otherwise be
    /// read after it was freed. Kept, it costs memory and never changes what a program prints.
    Bind void or failure to emit-pulled unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        If statement's kind is "PullStatement", cast one's emit-pulled-modules on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "BindStatement" and inner's kind is not "ObjectDefinition" and inner's kind is not "InterfaceDefinition":
                Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// The statements hoisting reaches: the top level and every pull's body, rabbits' included.
    Bind void to gather-hoisted, given (the node statements, the series of node found):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Insert statement into found.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement" or statement's kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast gather-hoisted on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), found).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `Judge <subject>, where it is:` over values — the subject held as `it`, each arm a test of it
    /// against its values, in order. An arm naming a type waits for a later slice.
    Bind void or failure to emit-judge unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define subject as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (subject) or pass the failure off.
        Define subject-kind as cast one's kind-of on (subject) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-union on (subject-kind):
            Cast one's emit-judge-union on (statement, subject-kind) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-scalar on (subject-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("judging a {subject-kind}")).
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("{cast c-type on (subject-kind)} cv_it = {value};").
        In one's kinds, the entry for "it" becomes subject-kind.
        Define first-arm as true.
        For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If the number of (cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children is greater than 0:
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a judgement arm naming a type")).
            Done.
            Define tests as "".
            For each written in (cast field-of on (arm, 5))'s children, repeat:
                Define written-kind as cast one's kind-of on (written) or pass the failure off.
                If written-kind is not subject-kind:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a judgement arm of another kind than its subject")).
                Done.
                Define test as cast c-equal on (subject-kind, "cv_it", cast one's c-of on (written) or pass the failure off).
                If tests is "", the tests becomes test.
                Otherwise, the tests becomes "{tests} || {test}".
            Done.
            If first-arm, cast one's line on ("if ({tests}) \{").
            Otherwise, cast one's line on ("\} else if ({tests}) \{").
            The first-arm becomes false.
            Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
            If first-arm:
                Cast one's line on ("\{").
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast one's line on ("\} else \{").
            Done.
            Cast one's emit-block on (otherwise-body) or pass the failure off.
            The first-arm becomes false.
        Done.
        If first-arm is false, cast one's line on ("\}").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// What this compiler cannot build in a function yet — a maker, a template or anything marked —
    /// or "". A method bound `unto` an object is built as that object's.
    Bind text or failure to function-beyond, given (the node statement):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 6)) is false, return "a maker".
        If the number of statement's children is greater than 8, return "a Bind with {(cast field-of on (statement, 9))'s word}".
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// A function's head as C: what it gives back, its name, and its parameters.
    /// `overrides` gives a parameter the kind a copy of the function was asked for; `named` is the
    /// copy's C name, or "" for the function's own.
    Bind text or failure to c-signature unto emitter, given (the node statement, the map from text to text overrides, the text named):
        Define gives as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define head as "void".
        If gives is not "void", the head becomes cast c-type on (gives).
        Define listing as "".
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define overridden as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) in overrides.
            If overridden is not void, the taken becomes overridden.
            If taken is "void", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a parameter of no type")).
            Define one-parameter as "{cast c-type on (taken)} {cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)))}".
            If listing is "", the listing becomes one-parameter.
            Otherwise, the listing becomes "{listing}, {one-parameter}".
        Done.
        If listing is "", the listing becomes "void".
        Define function-c as named.
        If function-c is "", the function-c becomes cast c-function-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))).
        Return "{head} {function-c}({listing})".
    Done.

    /// One function as C. A body sees its parameters and nothing of the program's top level.
    Bind text or failure to c-function unto emitter, given (the node statement, the map from text to text overrides, the text named):
        Define writer as cast one's sibling.
        In writer's kinds, the entry for "%return" becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define overridden as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) in overrides.
            If overridden is not void, the taken becomes overridden.
            In writer's kinds, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) becomes taken.
        Done.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            Cast writer's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define signature as cast one's c-signature on (statement, overrides, named) or pass the failure off.
        Return "{signature} \{\n{writer's body converted to text}\}\n\n".
    Done.

    /// The whole program as one C file: the series types, its objects, its functions and methods —
    /// declared first, so any may call any — then what it does.
    Bind text or failure to c-program, given (the node program):
        Define functions as a map from text to node.
        Define objects as a map from text to node.
        Define methods as a map from text to node.
        // Every method, by the object it belongs to: written inside it, or bound `unto` it.
        Define owned as a series of node.
        Define owners as a series of text.
        Define hoisted as a series of node.
        Cast gather-hoisted on (program, hoisted).
        Define interfaces as a map from text to node.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
                In interfaces, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes statement.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                Define beyond as cast object-beyond on (statement).
                If beyond is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond)).
                Define object-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                In objects, the entry for object-name becomes statement.
                For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                    Define beyond-method as cast function-beyond on (method) or pass the failure off.
                    If beyond-method is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond-method)).
                    In methods, the entry for "{object-name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}" becomes method.
                    Insert method into owned.
                    Insert object-name into owners.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement":
                Define beyond as cast function-beyond on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                If beyond is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond)).
                Define unto-target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
                If cast is-nothing on (unto-target):
                    In functions, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes statement.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Define object-name as cast unquoted on (unto-target).
                    If (the entry for object-name in objects) is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a method bound 'unto' {object-name}")).
                    In methods, the entry for "{object-name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))}" becomes statement.
                    Insert statement into owned.
                    Insert object-name into owners.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define writer as cast fresh-emitter on (functions, objects, methods, interfaces).
        For each pair in objects, repeat:
            Define conformance as cast writer's conformance-beyond on (the value of pair).
            If conformance is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (conformance)).
        Done.

        // The objects, each after those its fields hold.
        Define ordered as a series of text.
        Define already-ordered as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in objects, repeat:
            Cast writer's order-objects on (the key of pair, already-ordered, a map from text to fact, ordered) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // Each object's series type named first, then the structs, then what writes and compares
        // them, then each series of objects whole — so a node may hold a series of nodes.
        Define structs as a chase.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on ("object {object-name}").
            Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast writer's c-object-struct on (object-name) or pass the failure off into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast c-object-heads on (object-name) into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast c-series-helpers on ("object {object-name}") into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast writer's c-object on (object-name) or pass the failure off into structs.
        Done.

        Define declared as a chase.
        Define defined as a chase.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                // One that takes an interface is built only as the copies its calls ask for.
                Define interface-taking as cast writer's takes-interface on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                If interface-taking is false:
                    Insert "{cast writer's c-signature on (statement, a map from text to text, "") or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
                    Insert cast writer's c-function on (statement, a map from text to text, "") or pass the failure off into defined.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each method in owned, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define owner as item place of owners.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-method-signature on (owner, method) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-method on (owner, method) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is not "BindStatement" and statement's kind is not "ObjectDefinition":
                Cast writer's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Every copy a call asked for — a copy's own calls may ask for more.
        Define built-copies as 0.
        While built-copies is less than the number of writer's pending-functions, repeat:
            Increment built-copies by 1.
            Define copied as item built-copies of writer's pending-functions.
            Define copy-name as item built-copies of writer's pending-names.
            Define copy-kinds as item built-copies of writer's pending-kinds.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-signature on (copied, copy-kinds, copy-name) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-function on (copied, copy-kinds, copy-name) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        // Every union the program used, each with its series — after the objects they may hold.
        Define union-types as a chase.
        For each union in writer's union-order, repeat:
            Insert cast c-union-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Insert cast c-series-helpers on (union) into union-types.
        Done.
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "#include \"cufet-runtime.h\"\n\n" into out.
        Insert cast c-series-prelude into out.
        // A series of a union named ahead of the objects, which may hold one by its address — and
        // how it is written and compared, which an object's own writing calls.
        For each union in writer's union-order, repeat:
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (union).
            Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into out.
            Insert "static void {series-type}_write({series-type}* s);\n" into out.
            Insert "static int {series-type}_eq({series-type}* a, {series-type}* b);\n" into out.
        Done.
        Insert structs converted to text into out.
        Insert union-types converted to text into out.
        Insert declared converted to text into out.
        Insert "\n" into out.
        Insert defined converted to text into out.
        Insert "int main(int argc, char** argv) \{\n" into out.
        Insert "    cufet_set_args(argc, argv);\n" into out.
        Insert "    CUFET_STDOUT_BINARY();\n" into out.
        Insert "    cufet_watch_stack();\n" into out.
        Insert "    cufet_arena_push();\n" into out.
        Insert writer's body converted to text into out.
        Insert "    cufet_arena_pop();\n" into out.
        Insert "    return 0;\n" into out.
        Insert "\}\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.
Done.
